  "edits": [
    {
      "item": "1",
      "old": "the following analysis focuses on the binocular metrics.",
      "new": "the following \\revision{Off-site} analysis focuses on the binocular metrics. \\revision{The same four ablation configurations are further evaluated on EDID to examine whether the performance gains extend to an external dataset.}"
    },
    {
      "item": "4",
      "old": "The ablation results show that Adaptive Label-Feature Relevance Construction (ARC)",
      "new": "\\revision{To examine whether the module-level improvements observed on ODIR also occur on an external dataset, the four ablation configurations are evaluated in the ODIR-to-EDID setting. Training uses the ODIR D/G/M subset described in Section 4.1, and EDID provides the target evaluation images. The ResNet50 backbone, source data split, and evaluation metrics are kept consistent across the four configurations.}\n\n\\input{tables/src/table_edid_ablation_trans.tex}\n\n\\revision{\\mbox{\\tabref{tab:ablation-edid}} reports the results of these supplementary ablation evaluations. The best-observed image-level Final scores are 52.16 for ResNet50, 53.75 for ResNet50+DFE, 53.27 for ResNet50+ARC, and 55.42 for the joint model. The joint configuration improves Final by 3.26 points over the baseline and by 1.67 and 2.15 points over the DFE and ARC configurations, respectively. It achieves the highest Final in both the ODIR Off-site and external EDID ablations, supporting the value of the joint configuration for cross-dataset recognition.}\n\nThe ablation results show that Adaptive Label-Feature Relevance Construction (ARC)"
    },
    {
      "item": "summary_scope",
      "old": "The ablation results show that Adaptive Label-Feature Relevance Construction (ARC)",
      "new": "The \\revision{ODIR Off-site} ablation results show that Adaptive Label-Feature Relevance Construction (ARC)"
    }
  ],
